E('ulysses s grant|ulysses grant', 'Ulysses S. Grant was the Union’s top general in the Civil War and the 18th US President.', 'He lived from 1822 to 1885 and was president from 1869 to 1877.', 'He accepted Lee’s surrender at Appomattox in 1865.', 'As president he fought the Ku Klux Klan.', 'He wrote acclaimed memoirs while dying of cancer.', 'He is on the US fifty-dollar bill.')
E('robert e lee', 'Robert E. Lee was the leading Confederate general in the American Civil War.', 'He lived from 1807 to 1870.', 'He commanded the Army of Northern Virginia.', 'He won battles like Chancellorsville but lost at Gettysburg.', 'He surrendered at Appomattox in April 1865.', 'Many statues of him have been removed in recent years.')
E('james madison', 'James Madison was the fourth US President, called the “Father of the Constitution”.', 'He lived from 1751 to 1836 and was president from 1809 to 1817.', 'He drafted much of the Constitution and the Bill of Rights.', 'He led the US in the War of 1812.', 'He was the shortest US president, at about 1.63 metres.')
E('war of 1812', 'The War of 1812 was fought between the United States and Britain.', 'It lasted from 1812 to 1815.', 'Causes included British interference with American shipping.', 'British troops burned Washington, including the White House, in 1814.', 'The US national anthem was written during a battle at Baltimore.', 'It ended in a stalemate.')
E('white house', 'The White House is the home and office of the US President.', 'It was first occupied in 1800.', 'John Adams was its first resident.', 'It was burned by the British in 1814 and rebuilt.', 'It has 132 rooms.', 'Theodore Roosevelt officially named it the White House in 1901.')
E('star-spangled banner|us national anthem', 'The Star-Spangled Banner is the US national anthem.', 'Francis Scott Key wrote the words in 1814.', 'He was inspired by the US flag still flying after the bombardment of Fort McHenry.', 'It became the official anthem in 1931.')
E('london|history of london', 'London is the capital of the United Kingdom.', 'The Romans founded it as Londinium around AD 47.', 'It was largely destroyed by fire in 1666.', 'It was bombed heavily in the Blitz of 1940 and 1941.', 'It was the world’s largest city in the 19th century.', 'It has hosted the Olympics three times: 1908, 1948 and 2012.')
E('paris|history of paris', 'Paris is the capital of France.', 'It began as a Celtic settlement of the Parisii tribe; the Romans called it Lutetia.', 'It was rebuilt with grand boulevards by Baron Haussmann in the 19th century.', 'It was occupied by Germany from 1940 to 1944.', 'It is famous for the Louvre, the world’s most visited museum.')
E('new york|new york city|history of new york', 'New York City is the largest city in the United States.', 'It was founded by the Dutch as New Amsterdam in 1624.', 'The English took it in 1664 and renamed it.', 'It was briefly the US capital.', 'Millions of immigrants arrived through Ellis Island.', 'It is a world centre of finance and culture.')
E('jerusalem', 'Jerusalem is one of the oldest cities in the world and holy to Jews, Christians and Muslims.', 'It has been inhabited for over 5,000 years.', 'King David made it his capital around 1000 BC.', 'The Western Wall is the holiest place where Jews can pray.', 'The Church of the Holy Sepulchre marks the traditional site of Jesus’s crucifixion.', 'The Dome of the Rock and al-Aqsa Mosque stand on the Temple Mount.')
E('istanbul', 'Istanbul is Turkey’s largest city, spanning Europe and Asia.', 'It was founded as Byzantium around 660 BC.', 'It was renamed Constantinople in 330.', 'The Ottomans captured it in 1453.', 'It was formally renamed Istanbul in 1930.', 'Hagia Sophia is its most famous building.')
E('tokyo|edo', 'Tokyo is the capital of Japan.', 'It was a small fishing village called Edo until the 17th century.', 'It became the shogun’s capital in 1603.', 'It was renamed Tokyo, “eastern capital”, in 1868.', 'It was devastated by an earthquake in 1923 and bombing in 1945.', 'Its metro area is the most populous in the world.')
E('beijing', 'Beijing is the capital of China.', 'It has been a capital for most of the last 800 years.', 'Kublai Khan made it his capital, called Khanbaliq.', 'It contains the Forbidden City and Tiananmen Square.', 'It hosted the Summer Olympics in 2008 and the Winter Olympics in 2022.')
E('venice', 'Venice is an Italian city built on more than 100 islands in a lagoon.', 'It was founded in the 5th century by people fleeing invaders.', 'It became a rich trading republic.', 'Its canals serve as streets.', 'It was ruled by elected leaders called doges for over 1,000 years.', 'Rising water and floods threaten it today.')
E('troy archaeology|heinrich schliemann', 'Heinrich Schliemann was a German businessman who excavated the site believed to be Troy.', 'He dug at Hisarlik, in Turkey, from 1871.', 'He found many layers of cities.', 'His methods damaged the site.', 'He also excavated Mycenae in Greece.')
E('pompeii discovery|herculaneum', 'Herculaneum was a Roman town buried by Vesuvius along with Pompeii.', 'It was buried in AD 79.', 'It was covered by deep volcanic mud and ash.', 'Even wooden furniture and food survived.', 'Charred scrolls found there are now being read using AI and X-rays.')
E('easter rising', 'The Easter Rising was an armed rebellion in Ireland against British rule.', 'It took place in Dublin in April 1916.', 'It was crushed within a week.', 'Fifteen leaders were executed.', 'The executions turned public opinion towards independence.')
E('irish independence|michael collins irish', 'Most of Ireland won independence from Britain after the Irish War of Independence.', 'The war lasted from 1919 to 1921.', 'Michael Collins was a key leader.', 'The Anglo-Irish Treaty created the Irish Free State in 1922.', 'A civil war followed over the treaty.')
E('chinese new year|lunar new year', 'Chinese New Year, or the Spring Festival, celebrates the start of the lunar year.', 'It has been celebrated for thousands of years.', 'Each year is linked to one of 12 animals of the zodiac.', 'Families gather for a reunion dinner.', 'Red decorations and fireworks are said to scare off bad luck.')
E('christmas history', 'Christmas celebrates the birth of Jesus.', 'It has been celebrated on 25 December since at least the 4th century.', 'Many traditions come from older winter festivals.', 'Christmas trees became popular in Britain through Queen Victoria’s German husband, Albert.', 'Santa Claus is partly based on Saint Nicholas.')
E('halloween', 'Halloween is a festival on 31 October.', 'It comes from the ancient Celtic festival of Samhain.', 'Celts believed the boundary with the dead was thin that night.', 'Irish and Scottish immigrants brought it to America.', 'Carved turnips came before pumpkins.')
